  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n**Root cause (3 lines max):** In `swap()`, `amountIn` is calculated as the delta between current balance and reserves (`balance - (_reserve - amountOut)`), but prior `accruedLaunchpadFee` remains in the balance while reserves subtract it in `_update`. This makes prior fees appear as extra current input, inflating `amountIn` for same-block subsequent swaps. The K-invariant check and new fee accrual then use this inflated value, skewing math until fees distribute on next block's first `_update`.\n\n**Impacts:** \n- Swappers get worse rates (less output for same input) due to \"fake\" higher input in pricing/reserves.\n- New launchpad fees over-accrue (e.g., 0.1% fee on inflated input), diluting legitimate rewards.\n- Distorts pool invariants mid-block; potential MEV (frontrun to exploit skewed pricing) or DoS (force bad rates via timed swaps). High impact if high-volume pairs, as it affects all same-block users post-fee accrual.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/f43e1eedb65e7e0327cfaf4d7608a37d85d2fae7/contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol#L232-L252\n\n```solidity\nFile: 2025-08-gte-perps-2/contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n263:    function swap(uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out, address to, bytes calldata data) external lock {\n264:         if (amount0Out == 0 && amount1Out == 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_OUTPUT_AMOUNT\");\n265:         (uint112 _reserve0, uint112 _reserve1,) = getReserves(); // gas savings\n266:         if (amount0Out >= _reserve0 || amount1Out >= _reserve1) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n267: \n268:         uint256 balance0;\n269:         uint256 balance1;\n270:         {\n271:             // scope for _token{0,1}, avoids stack too deep errors\n272:             address _token0 = token0;\n273:             address _token1 = token1;\n274:             if (to == _token0 || to == _token1) revert(\"UniswapV2: INVALID_TO\");\n275:             if (amount0Out > 0) _safeTransfer(_token0, to, amount0Out); // optimistically transfer tokens\n276:             if (amount1Out > 0) _safeTransfer(_token1, to, amount1Out); // optimistically transfer tokens\n277:             if (data.length > 0) IUniswapV2Callee(to).uniswapV2Call(msg.sender, amount0Out, amount1Out, data);\n278:             balance0 = IERC20(_token0).balanceOf(address(this));\n279:             balance1 = IERC20(_token1).balanceOf(address(this));\n280:         }\n281:   >>>   uint256 amount0In = balance0 > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? balance0 - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0;\n282:   >>>   uint256 amount1In = balance1 > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? balance1 - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0;\n283:         if (amount0In == 0 && amount1In == 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n284: \n285:         {\n286:             // scope for reserve{0,1}Adjusted and launchpadFee{0,1}, avoids stack too deep errors\n287:             uint256 balance0Adjusted = balance0.mul(1000).sub(amount0In.mul(3));\n288:             uint256 balance1Adjusted = balance1.mul(1000).sub(amount1In.mul(3));\n289: \n290:             if (balance0Adjusted.mul(balance1Adjusted) < uint256(_reserve0).mul(_reserve1).mul(1000 ** 2)) {\n291:                 revert(\"UniswapV2: K\");\n292:             }\n293: \n294:             (uint112 launchpadFee0, uint112 launchpadFee1) = launchpadFeeDistributor > address(0)\n295:                 && rewardsPoolActive > 0 ? _getLaunchpadFees(amount0In, amount1In) : (uint112(0), uint112(0));\n296: \n297:             _update(balance0, balance1, _reserve0, _reserve1, launchpadFee0, launchpadFee1);\n298:         }\n299: \n300:         emit Swap(msg.sender, amount0In, amount1In, amount0Out, amount1Out, to);\n301:    \n\n```\n\n**Vulnerability flow (step-by-step with PoC math):**\n1. Setup: Pool has 100 ETH base/quote reserves, launchpad owns ~100% LP (totalSupply=100 ETH). No prior fees.\n2. First swap: User sends 10 ETH base input → pair balance_base=110 ETH. Swap outputs ~9.066 ETH quote (997/1000 fee). New fee0 = (10 * 1 * 100%) / (100 * 1000) = 0.01 ETH accrued. Reserves update to balance - totalFee0 = 110 - 0.01 = 109.99 ETH base (quote ~90.933 ETH). Event: `Swap(amount0In=10 ETH)`.\n3. Same-block second swap: User sends actual 10 ETH base → pair balance_base=120 ETH (110 prior + 10 new). But reserves still reflect prior subtraction (109.99 base), so detected amount0In = 120 - (109.99 - 0) = 10.01 ETH (actual 10 + prior 0.01 fee). Outputs ~7.557 ETH quote (worse rate due to skewed reserves). New fee0 = (10.01 * 1 * 100%) / (100 * 1000) ≈ 0.01001 ETH (over-accrued on inflation). Reserves: 120 - 0.02001 totalFee0 ≈ 119.979 ETH base. Event: `Swap(amount0In=10.01 ETH)` (verifies inflation).\n4. Next block: First `_update` (e.g., sync/swap) distributes 0.02001 ETH fees to distributor, resetting accrued=0 and aligning reserves=balances. Until then, mid-block swaps suffer distorted pricing.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\naccount for `accrued fees` before calculating the `amountIn` sent",
  "proof_of_concept": "<details>\n\n<summary> \nAttached POC (click to drop down)\n</summary>\n\n1. Replace `test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad.t.sol` completely as shown below\n2. then run  `forge t --mc PoCLaunchpad  -vvv`\n\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {MockDistributor} from \"../mocks/MockDistributor.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {IUniswapV2Pair} from \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IUniswapV2Pair.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is Test {\n    MockERC20 public base;\n    MockERC20 public quote;\n    GTELaunchpadV2Pair public pair;\n    address public launchpad;\n    MockDistributor public distributor;\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory public v2Factory;\n    address public mockERC20Logic;\n    address public token0;\n    address public token1;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        launchpad = makeAddr(\"launchpad\");\n        vm.label(launchpad, \"Launchpad\");\n\n        distributor = new MockDistributor();\n\n        v2Factory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), launchpad, launchpad, address(distributor));\n\n        mockERC20Logic = address(new MockERC20());\n\n        (address baseAddr, address quoteAddr, address pairAddr) = _createLaunchpadPair(\"base\", \"quote\");\n\n        base = MockERC20(baseAddr);\n        quote = MockERC20(quoteAddr);\n        pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(pairAddr);\n\n        deal(address(base), address(this), 100 ether);\n        deal(address(quote), address(this), 100 ether);\n\n        base.transfer(address(pair), 100 ether);\n        quote.transfer(address(pair), 100 ether);\n\n        token0 = pair.token0();\n        token1 = pair.token1();\n\n        // lp tokens are minted to launchpad as the fee calc is the launchpad's share of total lp supply\n        pair.mint(launchpad);\n    }\n\n    function _createLaunchpadPair(string memory nameBase, string memory nameQuote)\n        internal\n        returns (address baseAddr, address quoteAddr, address pairAddr)\n    {\n        baseAddr = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(nameBase))));\n        quoteAddr = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(nameQuote))));\n\n        if (baseAddr > quoteAddr) {\n            (baseAddr, quoteAddr) = (quoteAddr, baseAddr);\n            (nameBase, nameQuote) = (nameQuote, nameBase);\n        }\n\n        vm.label(baseAddr, string(abi.encodePacked(nameBase, \" Token\")));\n        vm.label(quoteAddr, string(abi.encodePacked(nameQuote, \" Token\")));\n\n        vm.etch(baseAddr, mockERC20Logic.code);\n        vm.etch(quoteAddr, mockERC20Logic.code);\n\n        MockERC20(baseAddr).initialize(nameBase, \"btn\", 18);\n        MockERC20(quoteAddr).initialize(nameQuote, \"qnt\", 18);\n\n        // Launchpad contract creates a pair\n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        v2Factory.createPair(baseAddr, quoteAddr);\n\n        pairAddr = v2Factory.getPair(baseAddr, quoteAddr);\n    }\n\n    function getAmountOut(uint256 amountIn, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut)\n        internal\n        pure\n        returns (uint256 amountOut)\n    {\n        require(amountIn > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveIn > 0 && reserveOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        uint256 amountInWithFee = amountIn * 997;\n        uint256 numerator = amountInWithFee * reserveOut;\n        uint256 denominator = (reserveIn * 1000) + amountInWithFee;\n        amountOut = numerator / denominator;\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair_, uint256 amountIn, address tokenIn)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out)\n    {\n        bool isZeroTokenIn = tokenIn == pair_.token0();\n        (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair_.getReserves();\n        (uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut) = isZeroTokenIn ? (reserve0, reserve1) : (reserve1, reserve0);\n        uint256 amountOut = getAmountOut(amountIn, reserveIn, reserveOut);\n        (amount0Out, amount1Out) = isZeroTokenIn ? (uint256(0), amountOut) : (amountOut, uint256(0));\n    }\n\n\n    /// @dev Test that the detected amountIn in swap includes previous accrued fees as extra input\n    function test_Swap_DetectedAmountInIncludesAccruedFee() public {\n        uint256 firstAmount = 10 ether;\n        deal(address(base), address(this), firstAmount);\n\n        (uint256 amount0Out1, uint256 amount1Out1) = getAmountsOut(pair, firstAmount, address(base));\n        base.transfer(address(pair), firstAmount);\n        pair.swap(amount0Out1, amount1Out1, address(this), hex\"\");\n\n        // Record previous accrued fee0\n        uint112 prevAccrued = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n        assertGt(uint256(prevAccrued), 0, \"No accrued fee after first swap\");\n\n        // Second swap, same direction\n        uint256 actualIn = 10 ether;\n        deal(address(base), address(this), actualIn);\n\n        (uint256 amount0Out2, uint256 amount1Out2) = getAmountsOut(pair, actualIn, address(base));\n\n        // Expected detected amount0In = actualIn + prevAccrued\n        uint256 expectedDetectedIn = actualIn + uint256(prevAccrued);\n\n        base.transfer(address(pair), actualIn);\n\n        // Expect the Swap event with extra amount0In\n        vm.expectEmit(true, false, false, true);\n        emit IUniswapV2Pair.Swap(\n            address(this),\n            expectedDetectedIn,\n            0,\n            0,\n            amount1Out2,\n            address(this)\n        );\n\n        pair.swap(0, amount1Out2, address(this), hex\"\");\n    }\n}\n\n\n\n\n```\n</details>",
